Return a 3-tuple from _get_per_token_logps_and_entropies for TRL >= 1.7.

TRL >= 1.7 extended _get_per_token_logps_and_entropies to return
(logps, entropies, aux_loss); all GRPOTrainer call sites unpack three
values. Upstream adopted the 3-tuple on the main return path (with a
version-aware downgrade for TRL < 1.7.0), but the compute_efficient
early-exit still returns a 2-tuple, crashing the first training step with

    ValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected 3, got 2)

whenever the efficient path is taken. Align it with the main return path.
(Rebased 2026-07-25: original hunk 2 dropped - merged upstream.
 Rebased 2026-10-19: same one-line fix, context moved to line 2473 at unsloth 6069a27a0.)
--- a/unsloth/models/rl_replacements.py
+++ b/unsloth/models/rl_replacements.py
@@ -2473,7 +2473,7 @@
         if compute_efficient:
             # No scoring forward may run (vLLM, beta = 0): latch precision here, not from the shared env.
             _unsloth_grpo_autocast(self)
-            return None, None
+            return None, None, None
         else:
             _unsloth_grpo_autocast(self)
 
